  "summary": "The math_and_collision scope contains three groups. (1) CollisionPrimitives: stateless math helpers - a ray-sphere quadratic intersection test feeding the vehicle suspension force calculation (0x00401180), a 2D direction projection (0x00423AD0) used in AI/opponent proximity, and an SSE two-point linear interpolation (0x0051F6A0). (2) CollisionModel: a collision-geometry container owning a 316-byte-stride strut array (+0x134, count +0x130), a 28-byte-stride struct array (+0x154) and further buffers (+0x150/+0x158); it supports nearest-neighbor queries over linked nodes and struts (0x00403640), indexed struct copies (0x00403F70), and a destructor-style teardown (0x004045F0) freeing every owned allocation. (3) SparseConstraintSolver: two standalone block LDL^T factorization and substitution-solve kernels (0x0056FA96, 0x00575BBD) operating on global double constraint-matrix workspaces and row-pointer tables, returning 0. All owners are UNKNOWN at the function-IR level; the classes above are DERIVED/GUESS proposals.",
